msgid "home.faq_help"
msgstr "Frequently Asked Questions and Help"

msgid "home.faq_1"
msgstr "Use unique names not only within one catalog, but also between them. That is, the name of a substance cannot be the same as a solution, mixture, or analysis name. Otherwise the program may work incorrectly!"

msgid "home.faq_2"
msgstr "A new recipe in the 'Recipes' section creates a recipe for both a solution and a mixture (which consists exclusively of dry substances). The required type must be selected in the form."

msgid "home.faq_3"
msgstr "If a solution recipe is used to account for a solution that is a component of other solutions - you need to check the box in the new recipe creation form 'Used as a component'."

msgid "home.faq_4"
msgstr "In the Warehouse section, aggregation of the Total amount for each reagent means that (Average price for all Warehouse Receipts and Expenses) * (Sum of quantities of all Receipts and Expenses) = Total amount. The same calculation applies to Solution Remainders. That is, Average price, Total amount per item - this is not an accurate accounting figure, but data for management accounting. To understand at what average accounting price and for approximately what amount there are remainders of a specific item."

msgid "home.faq_5"
msgstr "Warehouse income can be made with a minus sign in the Quantity field of the form. This can be useful when you need to adjust balances after inventory, when an excess of some reagent (substance) is found. Then the Price in the form should be average, which can be taken from the Warehouse section for this reagent."

msgid "home.faq_5_additional"
msgstr "Or at your own discretion. Keep in mind that zero price will change the average price!"

msgid "home.faq_6"
msgstr "For expense statistics display, keep in mind that the later date is not included. That is, if you need to view from March 15 to March 16, then select dates 03/15/2021 - 03/17/2021"

msgid "home.faq_7"
msgstr "Since the program works via the internet - it is advisable to periodically change the password, at least once every three months."

